abstract: >-
  A deduplicated cross-disciplinary dataset of 1,900 unsolved, open and hard
  problems across 8 Macro-Pillars, 28 Superdomains, 8 Physical/Formal Substrates and
  7 Abstraction Layers, linked in a 5,808-edge knowledge graph that a Python
  (NetworkX) audit finds biconnected (0 articulation points, 0 bridges, 0 dangling
  links). It includes 103 audited Lean 4.35.0 theorems without Mathlib about the
  atlas scoring software (integer bounds of the scoring formulas, monotonicity of CSS, Titan and leverage,
  quadrant and era maps, taxonomy list sizes, a generic list-multigraph handshaking
  lemma, a dedup bound and the AutoResearch keep/discard rule), kernel-checked by
  Lean, with the 9 Palomar comparator targets also accepted by six kernel checks
  (five distinct implementations); no Lean statement refers to the atlas data or its
  graph. Also included: a 10-page AMS-LaTeX white paper, offline SQLite FTS5 hybrid
  search (100.0% MRR@5 on 25 benchmark queries), an 11-tool stdio MCP server, a
  registry delta checker, 3 finite Track B probes, a rubric sensitivity diff tool
  and an AutoResearch evaluation harness (AQS = 97.99). None of the 1,900 problems
  is claimed solved.
